  "details": "I am one of the creators of the a mesh-based tracking follower system with a completely invisible mesh that scales to world size.  This mesh is never rendered visible to the player and has an invisible shader for both the main and fallback systems.  \n\nSomething changed in VRChat back-end in the last year that uses all meshes both visible and invisible to calculate avatar height.  This means that every avatar with this system is miscalculated as world size and puts the nameplate at max height.\n\nI would recommend that the avatar calculation not include invisible meshes when calculating nameplate height, like it was before.  Either that, or have a way for me to do something on my end to fix it.  My customers have been complaining that it is my fault and as far as I am aware, this is a bug.\n\nI would be happy to discuss this further if need be.  Feel free to reach out anytime.",
